// This Pine Script™ code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
//
// Wickless Candles (MTF) — marks candles with (within a small tolerance) no wick on one side,
// across five fixed timeframes at once: 1m, 5m, 15m, 1H, 4H. Operator's own ask (2026-10-22):
// "I need a tradingview indicator that will draw a line and label the chart time frame that has a
// wickless candle body on it," then: "I want it to mark out all wickless candles from the 1min
// 5min 15min 1hr and 4hr."
//
// DEFINITION — same tolerance-based rule already proven in the operator's own Quantower work
// (srmAutoStrategy / WicklessLevelEngine): a candle's body-extreme sits within a small tick
// tolerance of the bar's own high/low on that side. A top-wickless candle (no upper wick) marks
// its HIGH as a level; a bottom-wickless candle (no lower wick) marks its LOW. Tolerance is in
// TICKS (syminfo.mintick multiples), not a fixed price number, so one default works across any
// instrument/price scale — 1 tick is the same "basically no wick" standard already used there.
//
// UNTESTED-UNTIL-TOUCHED — same convention used throughout: each level extends forward from the
// candle that formed it until a LATER bar's range trades through that exact price (high >= level
// and low <= level — the exact wick touching it counts, same as a resting take-profit order would
// fill there). By default a tested level is DELETED outright (`showTestedInput` off) rather than
// kept dimmed — operator's own report, 2026-10-22: leaving every tested level on the chart piled
// up into unreadable clutter over a session. With `showTestedInput` on, it's kept instead — frozen,
// dimmed, relabeled with a "(tested)" suffix. Checked against the CURRENT chart's own high/low
// every bar, regardless of which of the five timeframes produced the level, so a touch is detected
// in real time no matter what timeframe you're viewing.
//
// LINES AND LABELS ARE PINNED INTO THE BLANK SPACE PAST THE LAST CANDLE (`last_bar_time + N *
// barInterval`, N staggered per timeframe) — same convention as the PWL/PDL/PML labels in the
// operator's own smc.pine, with the label itself using `label.style_label_left` so its text grows
// LEFTWARD from that fixed right-side anchor and never runs off the edge. Labels show just the
// timeframe + side (e.g. "1m WLS H") — no price in the text, since the line itself already sits at
// the exact price on the axis.
//
// MULTI-TIMEFRAME MECHANICS — non-repainting by construction: each timeframe's own bar count is
// read via `timeframe.change(tf)` (computable directly from the chart's own bar stream, no fetch
// needed), and its CONFIRMED (just-closed) OHLC is pulled via `request.security(..., open[1],
// high[1], low[1], close[1], time[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)` — the same "offset by one
// bar inside a lookahead_on request" idiom the operator's own smc.pine (LuxAlgo) uses for its Fair
// Value Gap detection. request.security's own timeframe argument must be a compile-time-constant
// string in Pine, so the five timeframes are five separate, explicit request.security calls
// (cannot be looped over a dynamic array of timeframe strings) — the actual per-timeframe
// detection/tracking logic is still written ONCE, in `processWickless()`, and just called five times.
//
// KNOWN LIMITATION, stated plainly: `request.security` can only return the LAST lower-timeframe bar
// within each bar of whatever chart you're actually viewing — so watching "1m" wickless candles
// while viewing a chart SLOWER than 1 minute (e.g. a 5-minute chart) will miss most of the 1-minute
// candles, not just the wickless ones. This is accurate and complete when viewed on the 1-minute
// chart itself (every one of the five requested timeframes is then >= the chart's own timeframe) —
// matches the operator's own stated primary use ("im going to use the 1min chart").
//
//@version=6
indicator('Wickless Candles (MTF)', shorttitle = 'Wickless MTF', overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// === Inputs ===
tolTicksInput = input.float(1.0, 'Wick tolerance (ticks, 0 = no wick at all)', minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = 'Detection')

show1m  = input.bool(true, '1 minute',  group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf1')
color1m = input.color(color.new(#ff6d00, 0), '', group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf1')
show5m  = input.bool(true, '5 minute',  group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf2')
color5m = input.color(color.new(#d500f9, 0), '', group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf2')
show15m = input.bool(true, '15 minute', group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf3')
color15m = input.color(color.new(#2979ff, 0), '', group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf3')
show1h  = input.bool(true, '1 hour',    group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf4')
color1h = input.color(color.new(#00c853, 0), '', group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf4')
show4h  = input.bool(true, '4 hour',    group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf5')
color4h = input.color(color.new(#ffd600, 0), '', group = 'Timeframes', inline = 'tf5')

maxLevelsPerTf = input.int(15, 'Max UNTESTED levels kept per timeframe', minval = 2, maxval = 80, group = 'Style', tooltip = 'Bounds how many still-untested levels each timeframe tracks at once.')
lineWidthInput = input.int(1, 'Line width', minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = 'Style')
showLabels     = input.bool(true, 'Show labels', group = 'Style')
showTestedInput = input.bool(false, 'Show tested levels (unchecked = delete them)', group = 'Style', tooltip = 'Off by default — a tested level is simply removed the instant price trades through it, instead of staying on the chart dimmed forever. With enough wickless candles in a session, leaving them all on the chart piles up into unreadable clutter once you scroll back.')
rightOffsetBars  = input.int(20, 'Right-edge offset (bars past the last candle)', minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = 'Style', tooltip = 'How far into the blank space past the last candle the lines/labels are pinned — same convention as the PWL/PDL/PML labels in smc.pine.')
labelStaggerBars = input.int(6, 'Label horizontal stagger (bars per timeframe)', minval = 0, maxval = 60, group = 'Style', tooltip = 'Each timeframe gets this many extra bars further right than the one before it (1m closest, 4h furthest), so two timeframes with a level at nearly the same price don\'t render their labels stacked on top of each other.')

tolerance = tolTicksInput * syminfo.mintick

// === Per-timeframe tracked state ===
// @type                     Tracks one timeframe's own untested wickless-top and wickless-bottom levels.
type tfState
    color    col
    line[]   topLines
    float[]  topLevels
    label[]  topLabels
    string[] topTexts
    line[]   botLines
    float[]  botLevels
    label[]  botLabels
    string[] botTexts

// @function      Builds one timeframe's tracked state with a fresh, independent set of arrays —
//                 `type` field defaults in Pine must be compile-time constants (na/false/literals),
//                 not function calls like array.new_line(), so each array is constructed explicitly
//                 here rather than as a UDT field default.
newTfState(color c) =>
    tfState.new(c, array.new_line(), array.new_float(), array.new_label(), array.new_string(), array.new_line(), array.new_float(), array.new_label(), array.new_string())

var tfState state1m  = newTfState(color1m)
var tfState state5m  = newTfState(color5m)
var tfState state15m = newTfState(color15m)
var tfState state1h  = newTfState(color1h)
var tfState state4h  = newTfState(color4h)

// === Core per-timeframe logic (called once per timeframe below) ===
// @function      Mitigation check (against the CURRENT chart's own high/low, every bar) + new-level
//                 creation (only on a freshly confirmed htf bar) for one timeframe's tracked arrays.
processWickless(tfState st, bool enabled, bool newBar, int htfTime, float o, float h, float l, float c, string tfTag, int slotIndex) =>
    // Pinned into the blank space past the last candle, same convention as smc.pine's own
    // PWL/PDL/PML labels (`last_bar_time + N * (time - time[1])`) — updates every bar so it tracks
    // the right edge as new candles form, rather than sitting at a fixed historical x. Each
    // timeframe gets its own extra stagger so same-price levels from different timeframes don't
    // land on the exact same spot.
    labelX = last_bar_time + ((rightOffsetBars + (slotIndex * labelStaggerBars)) * (time - time[1]))
    if enabled
        // A level this bar's range just traded through is "tested." Default: delete it outright
        // (line + label) rather than leave it on the chart — with enough wickless candles in a
        // session, keeping every tested one piles up into unreadable clutter once you scroll back
        // (operator's own report, 2026-10-22, with a screenshot showing exactly that). With
        // `showTestedInput` on, it's kept instead — frozen, dimmed, relabeled "(tested)" — using the
        // base text tracked in `topTexts`/`botTexts` ourselves rather than a label.get_text() getter.
        if array.size(st.topLines) > 0
            for i = array.size(st.topLines) - 1 to 0
                lvl = array.get(st.topLevels, i)
                if high >= lvl and low <= lvl
                    ln   = array.get(st.topLines, i)
                    lbl  = array.get(st.topLabels, i)
                    if showTestedInput
                        base = array.get(st.topTexts, i)
                        line.set_x2(ln, labelX)
                        line.set_color(ln, color.new(st.col, 75))
                        line.set_style(ln, line.style_dotted)
                        if not na(lbl)
                            label.set_x(lbl, labelX)
                            label.set_text(lbl, base + ' (tested)')
                    else
                        line.delete(ln)
                        if not na(lbl)
                            label.delete(lbl)
                    array.remove(st.topLines, i)
                    array.remove(st.topLevels, i)
                    array.remove(st.topLabels, i)
                    array.remove(st.topTexts, i)
                else
                    line.set_x2(array.get(st.topLines, i), labelX)

        if array.size(st.botLines) > 0
            for i = array.size(st.botLines) - 1 to 0
                lvl = array.get(st.botLevels, i)
                if high >= lvl and low <= lvl
                    ln   = array.get(st.botLines, i)
                    lbl  = array.get(st.botLabels, i)
                    if showTestedInput
                        base = array.get(st.botTexts, i)
                        line.set_x2(ln, labelX)
                        line.set_color(ln, color.new(st.col, 75))
                        line.set_style(ln, line.style_dotted)
                        if not na(lbl)
                            label.set_x(lbl, labelX)
                            label.set_text(lbl, base + ' (tested)')
                    else
                        line.delete(ln)
                        if not na(lbl)
                            label.delete(lbl)
                    array.remove(st.botLines, i)
                    array.remove(st.botLevels, i)
                    array.remove(st.botLabels, i)
                    array.remove(st.botTexts, i)
                else
                    line.set_x2(array.get(st.botLines, i), labelX)

        // New confirmed htf bar — check wickless conditions and arm a fresh level if it qualifies.
        if newBar and not na(o)
            bodyHigh = math.max(o, c)
            bodyLow  = math.min(o, c)

            if (h - bodyHigh) <= tolerance
                baseTxt  = tfTag + ' WLS H'
                newLine  = line.new(htfTime, h, labelX, h, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = st.col, width = lineWidthInput, style = line.style_solid)
                label newLabel = na
                if showLabels
                    newLabel := label.new(labelX, h, baseTxt, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = st.col, size = size.small)
                array.push(st.topLines, newLine)
                array.push(st.topLevels, h)
                array.push(st.topLabels, newLabel)
                array.push(st.topTexts, baseTxt)
                if array.size(st.topLines) > maxLevelsPerTf
                    oldLine  = array.shift(st.topLines)
                    array.shift(st.topLevels)
                    oldLabel = array.shift(st.topLabels)
                    array.shift(st.topTexts)
                    line.delete(oldLine)
                    if not na(oldLabel)
                        label.delete(oldLabel)

            if (bodyLow - l) <= tolerance
                baseTxt  = tfTag + ' WLS L'
                newLine  = line.new(htfTime, l, labelX, l, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = st.col, width = lineWidthInput, style = line.style_solid)
                label newLabel = na
                if showLabels
                    newLabel := label.new(labelX, l, baseTxt, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = st.col, size = size.small)
                array.push(st.botLines, newLine)
                array.push(st.botLevels, l)
                array.push(st.botLabels, newLabel)
                array.push(st.botTexts, baseTxt)
                if array.size(st.botLines) > maxLevelsPerTf
                    oldLine  = array.shift(st.botLines)
                    array.shift(st.botLevels)
                    oldLabel = array.shift(st.botLabels)
                    array.shift(st.botTexts)
                    line.delete(oldLine)
                    if not na(oldLabel)
                        label.delete(oldLabel)

// === Five explicit, literal-timeframe requests — request.security's own timeframe argument must
// be a compile-time constant in Pine, so this can't be a loop over a dynamic array of strings. ===
//
// 1m is special-cased: when the chart itself IS the 1-minute chart, requesting "1" via
// request.security is asking for the exact same series the chart already has — a redundant,
// self-referential request that produced mismatched OHLC in practice (operator's own report,
// 2026-10-22: a candle with a visible wick got flagged wickless, and the resulting bad level also
// never tested/deleted correctly — both symptoms point at the SAME corrupted fetch). Bypassed
// entirely by using the chart's own native open[1]/high[1]/low[1]/close[1]/time[1] whenever
// timeframe.period == '1', with newBar1m simply always true in that case (every closed chart bar
// IS a new 1-minute bar when the chart itself is 1-minute). The request.security call still runs
// unconditionally either way — Pine doesn't allow skipping it based on a runtime branch — its
// result is just ignored on the native path.
isNative1m = timeframe.period == '1'
[sec_time1m, sec_open1m, sec_high1m, sec_low1m, sec_close1m] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '1', [time[1], open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
newBar1m = isNative1m ? true : timeframe.change('1')
time1m   = isNative1m ? time[1]  : sec_time1m
open1m   = isNative1m ? open[1]  : sec_open1m
high1m   = isNative1m ? high[1]  : sec_high1m
low1m    = isNative1m ? low[1]   : sec_low1m
close1m  = isNative1m ? close[1] : sec_close1m

newBar5m = timeframe.change('5')
[time5m, open5m, high5m, low5m, close5m] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '5', [time[1], open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

newBar15m = timeframe.change('15')
[time15m, open15m, high15m, low15m, close15m] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '15', [time[1], open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

newBar1h = timeframe.change('60')
[time1h, open1h, high1h, low1h, close1h] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '60', [time[1], open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

newBar4h = timeframe.change('240')
[time4h, open4h, high4h, low4h, close4h] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '240', [time[1], open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

processWickless(state1m,  show1m,  newBar1m,  time1m,  open1m,  high1m,  low1m,  close1m,  '1m',  0)
processWickless(state5m,  show5m,  newBar5m,  time5m,  open5m,  high5m,  low5m,  close5m,  '5m',  1)
processWickless(state15m, show15m, newBar15m, time15m, open15m, high15m, low15m, close15m, '15m', 2)
processWickless(state1h,  show1h,  newBar1h,  time1h,  open1h,  high1h,  low1h,  close1h,  '1H',  3)
processWickless(state4h,  show4h,  newBar4h,  time4h,  open4h,  high4h,  low4h,  close4h,  '4H',  4)

// === Alerts — generic across all five timeframes rather than ten granular ones ===
top1m  = show1m  and newBar1m  and not na(open1m)  and (high1m  - math.max(open1m,  close1m))  <= tolerance
top5m  = show5m  and newBar5m  and not na(open5m)  and (high5m  - math.max(open5m,  close5m))  <= tolerance
top15m = show15m and newBar15m and not na(open15m) and (high15m - math.max(open15m, close15m)) <= tolerance
top1h  = show1h  and newBar1h  and not na(open1h)  and (high1h  - math.max(open1h,  close1h))  <= tolerance
top4h  = show4h  and newBar4h  and not na(open4h)  and (high4h  - math.max(open4h,  close4h))  <= tolerance
anyNewTop = top1m or top5m or top15m or top1h or top4h

bot1m  = show1m  and newBar1m  and not na(open1m)  and (math.min(open1m,  close1m)  - low1m)  <= tolerance
bot5m  = show5m  and newBar5m  and not na(open5m)  and (math.min(open5m,  close5m)  - low5m)  <= tolerance
bot15m = show15m and newBar15m and not na(open15m) and (math.min(open15m, close15m) - low15m) <= tolerance
bot1h  = show1h  and newBar1h  and not na(open1h)  and (math.min(open1h,  close1h)  - low1h)  <= tolerance
bot4h  = show4h  and newBar4h  and not na(open4h)  and (math.min(open4h,  close4h)  - low4h)  <= tolerance
anyNewBottom = bot1m or bot5m or bot15m or bot1h or bot4h

alertcondition(anyNewTop, title = 'Wickless Top formed', message = 'Wickless top candle formed (no upper wick) on a watched timeframe.')
alertcondition(anyNewBottom, title = 'Wickless Bottom formed', message = 'Wickless bottom candle formed (no lower wick) on a watched timeframe.')
